/**
 * @file raymath.angel
 * @details These functions go around the problem that Vector2 cannot be used as a value
 * type on linux.
 * When AngelScript is used as CPP then these are not used, but the actual
 * CPP function is called
 * @note
 * This file contains raymath code modified to work with AngelScript language.
 * Modified by muffintrap
 * - Added classes for Vector2, -3, -4, Quaternion and Matrix
 * - Changed {0,0,0} style Vector constructors to named constructors
 * - Implemented Equals functions with AngelScript's built-in closeTo() function
 * - Added {} to all if clauses
 * - Removed explicit casts to float in matrix functions
 * - Changed arrays to AngelScript syntax
 */

